Why would a Tesla-SpaceX merger make raising money easier? 

@altcap Brad Gerstner says Elon wants scale now, because one bigger company can borrow more cheaply to fund all this CapEx.

@TeslaLarry puts the number at half a trillion dollars for 10 GW of compute, and closer to $1T for 20 GW. That's about 3% of US GDP, more than any single private company has ever borrowed. Lenders are already hitting their limits on how much they can lend one borrower.

A bigger combined company brings more assets and cash flow, and spreads the risk across more lenders, which means easier terms. 

$TSLA $SPCX

